1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
Stacking pennies to the fucking Moon is cheaper than you think.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:07,760
Here's the setup. One penny is about one and a half millimeters thick.

3
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:11,600
The Moon is about two hundred thirty-nine thousand miles away.

4
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:15,300
We're pretending the stack stands perfectly straight. It never would.

5
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:19,340
So how many pennies is that? About two hundred fifty-three billion.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,320
Double-tap if your brain just blue-screened a little bit.

7
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,160
Now, a hundred pennies make one dollar.

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,740
So the whole damn tower costs about two point five three billion dollars.

9
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:33,980
That's barely more than the biggest lottery jackpot ever, which was about two billion.

10
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:37,100
One lucky Powerball ticket, and you're most of the way to space.

11
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,860
Send this to the friend who still keeps a coin jar.

12
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:43,280
Now swap the pennies for dollar bills. Should be cheaper, right?

13
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:48,120
Nope. A bill is paper thin, so you need a ridiculous number of them.

14
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,920
A stack of dollar bills to the Moon costs about thirty-five trillion dollars.

15
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:54,700
Follow, 'cause it gets even dumber.

16
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,740
That's around seventeen thousand record jackpots.

17
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:02,640
Meanwhile, the penny tower split across everyone on Earth is thirty-one cents each.

18
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:06,400
So the coin everyone ignores is the cheapest ride to the Moon.

19
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:09,500
Would you chip in your thirty-one cents? Yes or no.

